    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.diff\n\n### Description\n\nCurrently, after enabling overlay, the extmarks are not set until the starting line of a hunk is visible on the screen. Sometimes, however, the hunk is still partially visible on the screen and I think it will be better if the highlights can be applied without requiring the user to scroll up to the starting line.\n\nI'm demonstrating the issue in the screencast below using the built-in `gen_source.save()` source:\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/52aa9d69-e9ba-4f6f-8dd6-25f95b6cab83\n\nSteps:\n1. Create a hunk spanning 2 lines\n2. Scroll down so that only the 2nd line is visible in the viewport\n3. Run `MiniDiff.toggle_overlay()` and observe that the hunk is not highlighted\n4. Scroll back up to the first line and observe that the hunk is highlighted\n5. Scroll back down and edit the 2nd line. Observe that highlight is removed\n6. Scroll back up and observe that highlight is applied again\n\nThe documentation mentions that manual scrolling is required for virtual lines above line 1, but since this issue can occur on other lines as well, it is not obvious whether it is the intended behavior of the plugin or not.\n\nUnderstandably, this issue only affects `overlay_lines` of types `add` and `change`, but not `change_worddiff` or `delete`, so it might not be of high priority, but I'll be happy to work on a PR if it aligns with the plugin's vision.",
