            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "This should now be fixed on the latest `main`.\n\nThe issue was that highlighting of buffer lines was done via a single extmark located at the top line of the hunk. As overlay rendering is done \"on demand\" (only when the target line is visible), it resulted in overlay highlighting showing only if the top hunk line is visible.\n\nThe change was to highlight every buffer line with a separate extmark. This results in a (hopefully) a bit more of an overhead in terms of the number of extmarks, but it shouldn't be too problematic due to described earlier \"on demand\" highlighting.",
